An application does ask for a row view, and nil costs it a whole column.

-[NSTableView rowViewAtRow:makeIfNecessary:] returned nil unconditionally. The note beside it said
that whether any application ASKS is what decides how much of this is worth building, and that iA
Writer asks zero times. iTerm2 asks for every row of its Advanced settings table, and its own
disassembly says exactly what nil costs:

  callq  *objc_msgSend        ; [tableView rowViewAtRow:row makeIfNecessary:NO]
  testq  %rax, %rax
  je     ...                  ; IF NIL, SKIP THE NEXT TWO
         interiorBackgroundStyle
         setBackgroundStyle:

-[iTermTableViewTextField setBackgroundStyle:] is what applies the regular or selected attributed
string the application handed the field earlier, through its own setRegularAttributedString: and
setSelectedAttributedString:. Skipping it left every description field empty. That is why the pane
drew its values and NONE of its descriptions, and why no text setter was ever called on those
fields at all: the application was waiting for a row view that never came.

  before   5 text setter calls in the run, every one a value
  after   13, including setAttributed len=245, len=243, len=27

and the pane now draws every setting name with its explanation beside its control.

NSTableRowView was a forwarding stub, so every message answered nil, and -interiorBackgroundStyle
answering nil happens to mean NSBackgroundStyleNormal, which is right for an unselected row and
wrong for the selected one. Selection is the only state that property depends on, so it is stored
and answered rather than left to the forwarder.

WHAT THIS IS AND IS NOT, because the gap matters to whoever reads it next. It vends a real
NSTableRowView per row, cached, with the row frame and the current selection, which answers what
applications ask a row view. It is NOT the macOS container: this table adds cell views to ITSELF,
not to a row view, so the vended view holds no subviews and is deliberately not inserted into the
hierarchy. Anything walking it expecting cell views inside will still find none. Associated storage
is used on both sides so no AppKit header changes and the rebuild stays small.

Gates: dts 69 of 69, patch record PASS, roster sweep 7 of 7 CONTENT and all seven unchanged against
the capture baseline, roster input 7 of 7, with iA Writer looked at because its library is the
heaviest table in the roster.

